Source: cerberus
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Paul Kilar <pkilar@gmail.com>
# Go >= 1.26 must be on PATH at build time. It is intentionally NOT expressed as
# a build dependency: the toolchain the code needs (1.26) is newer than the
# distro's golang-go, so builds use an upstream Go (e.g. the golang:1.26 image or
# a manually installed toolchain). go.mod's `go 1.26.0` is the real floor and
# `go build` fails loudly on an older toolchain.
#
# debhelper (>= 13.6~) is required because rules explicitly invokes
# dh_installsysusers (added in 13.6); the bare compat-13 pin is otherwise
# satisfied by 13.3 (Debian 11 bullseye), where that helper does not exist.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), debhelper (>= 13.6~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/pkilar/cerberus
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: cerberus-api
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: krb5-user
Description: SSH certificate authority API service for AWS Nitro Enclaves
 Cerberus is an SSH Certificate Authority whose CA private key lives only
 inside an AWS Nitro Enclave. This package provides the host-side HTTPS
 gateway service: it authenticates requests with Kerberos/SPNEGO (and,
 optionally, OIDC bearer tokens), enforces per-group authorization, forwards
 signing requests to the enclave over VSOCK, and performs the attested KMS
 Decrypt on the enclave's behalf (the enclave has no network of its own).
 .
 The service is designed for an AWS Nitro-enabled EC2 host running the
 cerberus-signer enclave.

Package: cerberus-signer
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
# No Recommends on aws-nitro-enclaves-cli: AWS ships it for Amazon Linux only,
# so on Debian/Ubuntu the name never resolves and apt reports it unsatisfiable
# forever. The requirement is real and is documented in
# cerberus-signer.README.Debian, which also covers building nitro-cli from
# source.
Description: SSH certificate signer that runs inside an AWS Nitro Enclave
 Cerberus is an SSH Certificate Authority whose CA private key lives only
 inside an AWS Nitro Enclave. This package provides the signer service: the
 signer binary, the enclave-lifecycle wrapper, the Dockerfile used to build
 the Enclave Image File (EIF), and the systemd unit launching the enclave.
 .
 The signer receives the host-mediated, attested KMS Decrypt result over
 VSOCK, decrypts the CMS envelope to install the in-memory CA signer, and
 signs SSH certificates. Running it needs aws-nitro-enclaves-cli (nitro-cli)
 and a Nitro-enabled EC2 host; the EIF itself is per-deployment and not
 shipped here (see cerberus-signer-eif).

Package: cerberus-vsock-watch
Architecture: amd64 arm64
# `auditd`, not `audit`: `audit` is the Arch package name and does not exist in
# Debian, which made this package uninstallable (`Depends: audit but it is not
# installable`).
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, auditd
Description: VSOCK-connect detective control for the Cerberus enclave boundary
 Detects an AF_VSOCK connect() to the Cerberus enclave from any process other
 than the legitimate cerberus-api — the signal that something on the host
 bypassed Casbin authorization and is attempting to mint SSH certificates
 directly against the enclave (docs/THREAT-MODEL.md SIGN-1). Runs an
 auditd-based detector and an eBPF tracepoint probe independently, ships
 alerts to a structured log and, optionally, an external webhook, and pings
 an external heartbeat endpoint so tampering with the detectors themselves is
 also observable.
 .
 This is a detective, not preventive, control: no host-side mechanism can
 fully prevent a process with host root from dialing the enclave directly.
 See docs/vsock-connect-detection.md.

Package: cerberus-client
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, openssh-client, curl, jq, krb5-user
Description: cssh SSH client helper (bash and zsh) for Cerberus
 The cssh shell wrapper for end-user workstations. Using the caller's
 Kerberos credentials (or an OIDC device-flow login), it fetches a
 short-lived OpenSSH user certificate from the Cerberus signing API, caches
 it next to the matching private key as <key>-cert.pub, and hands off to
 ssh(1), re-signing only when the cached cert is missing or about to expire.
 .
 Installed as /etc/profile.d/cssh.sh; it defines the cssh function for login
 shells. Set the site endpoint with CERBERUS_URL in the companion
 /etc/profile.d/cerberus-env.sh. See /usr/share/doc/cerberus-client/cssh.md.

Package: cerberus-signer-eif
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Build-Profiles: <pkg.cerberus.eif>
Depends: cerberus-signer (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Enclave Image File for the Cerberus signer (per-deployment)
 Prebuilt Nitro Enclave Image File for the Cerberus signer, installed at
 /usr/share/cerberus/ssh-cert-signer.eif.
 .
 CONDITIONAL and per-deployment: the EIF bakes in the KMS-encrypted CA private key
 and a PCR0-pinned CA public key, so this package carries CA key material and
 pins a deployment-specific PCR0. It is per-architecture and must be
 distributed only over an operator-controlled channel, never a shared or
 public repository. Built only under the pkg.cerberus.eif build profile
 (build-deb.sh --eif <path>).
